WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.960
- I placed my daughter for adoption at 19.

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:05.973
Should I tell her I'm her birth mom?

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:09.653
Yes or no?

00:00:11.439 --> 00:00:14.356
(compelling music)

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:32.460
- I feel like there's so many
factors that go into this.

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:34.590
It's not as simple, like, yes or no.

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:35.850
Something like this could really,

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:37.290
like, shake their whole world.

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:38.400
And are you healthy?

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:39.840
Are you healthy enough to be

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:41.730
in her life right now? You know?

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:43.710
And it's just a lot.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:46.050
- I'm kind of in the middle because, like,

00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:48.240
if the child wants to reach out

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:50.513
to know their birth mom, 100%.

00:00:50.513 --> 00:00:53.340
- I think that perhaps she
should have a conversation

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:57.507
with the parents first and
make sure that they know,

00:00:57.507 --> 00:01:00.843
and then getting their consent, basically.

00:01:01.843 --> 00:01:03.780
(beep)

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:06.630
- I see my 11 year old daughter often.

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:08.580
And she doesn't know I'm her birth mom.

00:01:10.512 --> 00:01:11.850
- Oh.
- Ooh.

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:14.153
- [Director] Does that
change any of your minds?

00:01:17.730 --> 00:01:21.240
- So after hearing that,
that she's 11 years old,

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:24.750
I changed my mind because she's young.

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:27.653
If she had been 18, it'd
be a different story.

00:01:27.653 --> 00:01:29.430
- I think I wanna go over here.

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:30.990
It's the 11 part that's like..

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.043
- I'm like you. I'm, like, in the middle.

00:01:32.043 --> 00:01:34.197
- It's very much in the middle.

00:01:34.197 --> 00:01:35.220
- Because..
- I'm coming over.

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:36.240
She's so young.

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:38.760
And to, like, get thrown
that information at 11,

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:42.570
it could go negatively, positively.

00:01:42.570 --> 00:01:45.560
And I feel like... (sighs)

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:48.570
- Well, if we take out
the age, and we say...

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:50.820
'cuz we didn't say she
has to tell her this week.

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:54.240
So how would y'all feel
about telling her, you know,

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:57.630
when she's 18 or whatever,
just at any point.

00:01:57.630 --> 00:02:00.750
- Yeah, but think of yourself,
like, as an 11 year old

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:01.890
And think of yourself as, like,

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:03.990
a 17, 18 year old finding it out.

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:07.963
I personally would rather
find out at 11 than 18

00:02:07.963 --> 00:02:08.796
- I think I'm gonna switch.

00:02:08.796 --> 00:02:10.140
- 'Cause then I would get more upset.

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:11.700
- I'm gonna switch. (laughter)

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:12.810
I'm gonna switch.

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:15.210
When I think about 11,
she's still innocent.

00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:16.920
She's still got that innocent in her.

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:19.110
By the time she's 13, we're...

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:22.710
our periods, our boobs are
coming, our minds are all...

00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:25.830
We already got enough
problems at 13, okay?

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:28.740
- How I see it is I did
have an 11 year old boy

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:31.300
that I had in my life who

00:02:32.992 --> 00:02:35.190
(laughs) was asked to be put

00:02:35.190 --> 00:02:38.460
into me and my ex-husband's life.

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:39.990
And he knew everything.

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:42.810
And how he saw it is he was happy

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:45.270
that there was somebody
else who loved him.

00:02:45.270 --> 00:02:47.490
Why is it a bad thing that
there was another person

00:02:47.490 --> 00:02:49.500
who loved this little girl so much

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:51.360
that she wanted to give her a better life?

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:53.970
Why not give that positive aspect to her?

00:02:53.970 --> 00:02:55.860
Like, I am another person who loves you

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:57.180
and has been watching out for you

00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:59.854
from afar like a guardian angel.

00:02:59.854 --> 00:03:01.860
(beep)

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:06.270
- If I reveal my identity,
my birth daughter could

00:03:06.270 --> 00:03:09.510
possibly have a relationship
with her half brother,

00:03:09.510 --> 00:03:10.503
my 10 month old.

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:15.923
- [Director] At this point,
does that change anyone's minds?

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:19.020
- Welcome back.

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:21.720
- Being a parent and...

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:23.550
you know, I went through surrogacy

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:25.590
but possibly have gone
through adoption before.

00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:27.660
And even when we were
going through adoption,

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:30.270
we were always like, yes,
we're always gonna tell

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:33.330
this kid where they come
from, who their parents are

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:35.460
so that we can be open in communication.

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:36.293
- Right.

00:03:36.293 --> 00:03:39.690
- But that was our decision
in the process being a parent.

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:44.690
So these parents now who
have taken over the adoption,

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:47.040
they have a right to be able to say

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:48.690
whether or not they wanna know.

00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:49.800
- Yeah, I second that.

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:52.200
I feel like a huge part
of identity is just

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:53.430
knowing where you come from.

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:56.670
And it's almost
counterproductive to her growth

00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:59.160
and her development to,
like, not be enlightened

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:01.170
of, like, where she comes from, you know?

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:04.110
- I moved because I'm personally adopted.

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:06.810
And I don't know how I would feel knowing

00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:09.270
that my birth mom was in my life

00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:11.940
for so long and knowing I was adopted

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:13.650
and just, like, having all those questions

00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:16.200
and just not getting the
answers and my mom lying to me.

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:17.370
So I just feel like

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:20.640
if you're open and
honest now, it's better.

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:21.473
- They'll understand.

00:04:21.473 --> 00:04:23.197
But it's not traumatizing as much...

00:04:23.197 --> 00:04:24.030
- Yeah.

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:24.863
- As, like, 18.

00:04:24.863 --> 00:04:26.610
And you already got your life going.

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:27.443
- Right.
- Exactly.

00:04:27.443 --> 00:04:29.220
And you did it for a reason, I assume.

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:31.440
Like, I believe my birth
mom put me up for adoption

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:32.970
because she couldn't take care of me.

00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:36.300
And I have this amazing life
now because of that decision.

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:38.550
Of course, there was some
resentment and, like, ah,

00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:39.870
you didn't want me, da, da, da.

00:04:39.870 --> 00:04:42.210
But, like, when I got older and stuff,

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:45.000
I realized that it was
all for the best of me.

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:47.250
And that's also a big thing.

00:04:47.250 --> 00:04:50.400
So kudos to you.

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:52.920
That was definitely a
hard decision, I believe.

00:04:52.920 --> 00:04:56.340
- As someone who has three half siblings

00:04:56.340 --> 00:04:57.600
who I love with all my heart,

00:04:57.600 --> 00:04:59.490
but, like, I wish I had
a stronger relationship

00:04:59.490 --> 00:05:01.470
with them and did not
get to grow up with them,

00:05:01.470 --> 00:05:03.150
I feel like adding that value

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:05.730
to the child's life would be amazing.

00:05:05.730 --> 00:05:08.040
- I think what keeps me
here, like, I like what a lot

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:10.290
of you guys are saying
and what we're saying too.

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:12.570
This needs to include the parents

00:05:12.570 --> 00:05:14.220
because the child could also have

00:05:14.220 --> 00:05:17.891
other brothers and sisters
in the child's new family.

00:05:17.891 --> 00:05:19.950
(beep)

00:05:19.950 --> 00:05:22.170
- I specifically chose a gay couple,

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:25.650
so she has two dads, with the intention

00:05:25.650 --> 00:05:28.110
of not having the issue
of the mother later

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:30.213
because I knew I wanted to be in her life.

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:34.380
I have gotten permission
from them multiple times

00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:37.080
and was given that as, like, one

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:39.210
of the criterias of the adoption.

00:05:39.210 --> 00:05:41.580
And I am treading extremely
lightly around them.

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:44.968
And they just continue to
choose to not tell her.

00:05:44.968 --> 00:05:46.950
(beep)

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:48.870
- I think naturally, she's gonna

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:50.490
have questions about her mom.

00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:52.020
She's getting to the age where, like,

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:53.670
she's gonna hit puberty and be like,

00:05:53.670 --> 00:05:57.480
oh, you guys don't know about periods.

00:05:57.480 --> 00:05:59.400
How do I do this?

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:01.050
What female...

00:06:01.050 --> 00:06:03.060
- I don't think you
should say that. (laughs)

00:06:03.060 --> 00:06:04.950
That's problematic. (laughs)

00:06:04.950 --> 00:06:05.783
- [Leesie] Okay. Wait, wait, wait.

00:06:05.783 --> 00:06:07.066
- [Kiohona] Because they're
two gay guys that...

00:06:07.066 --> 00:06:07.899
- Wait. Are we asking questions or...

00:06:07.899 --> 00:06:09.240
- That they won't be able to,

00:06:09.240 --> 00:06:10.680
you know, be able to tell her how

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:12.464
to take care of herself.

00:06:12.464 --> 00:06:13.297
- That's true.

00:06:13.297 --> 00:06:14.130
- I'm pretty sure that they had...

00:06:14.130 --> 00:06:14.963
- I meant, like, the way, like...

00:06:14.963 --> 00:06:15.796
- I would hope so.

00:06:15.796 --> 00:06:17.880
- Like putting in a tampon, you know?

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:20.093
- Yeah, I mean, that's
what they signed up for,

00:06:20.093 --> 00:06:22.080
to have a little girl, is to show her

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:23.310
how to take care of herself.

00:06:23.310 --> 00:06:25.710
- I'm curious, what is their reason

00:06:25.710 --> 00:06:28.830
for not wanting to let you tell them?

00:06:28.830 --> 00:06:30.420
- They haven't given me one.

00:06:30.420 --> 00:06:32.160
I've been told it will happen.

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:34.410
Multiple times, it's been,

00:06:34.410 --> 00:06:35.910
oh, she's starting to ask questions.

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:37.620
We should sit down and talk about it.

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:39.180
And then when I set up the meeting,

00:06:39.180 --> 00:06:40.500
we don't discuss it.

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:43.140
- Okay, that changes my mind.

00:06:43.140 --> 00:06:44.670
I think that's not fair

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:46.770
that they're not giving
a timeframe for you.

00:06:46.770 --> 00:06:48.990
I plan to have kids myself too.

00:06:48.990 --> 00:06:50.160
And I'm not gonna lie to them.

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:51.990
You know, two guys, we can't make a child.

00:06:51.990 --> 00:06:55.620
So I'm gonna say, like, there
is a woman that is your mom.

00:06:55.620 --> 00:06:57.960
- I'm gay. And I have a husband,

00:06:57.960 --> 00:06:59.250
and I have two daughters.

00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:01.860
Our two girls know everything.

00:07:01.860 --> 00:07:04.380
We've told them everything.
They know everything.

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:06.930
I don't know the reason why
they're not telling her.

00:07:06.930 --> 00:07:10.800
All I know is that as a gay man

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:13.800
who has two daughters

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:16.410
and who are constantly, you know,

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:19.410
having comments like that come to us like,

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:21.750
oh, what are you gonna
do when they turn 13?

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:24.030
Because, you know, you don't know.

00:07:24.030 --> 00:07:25.200
You know, you're not a woman.

00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:27.060
You don't know these things.

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:29.100
I have many strong women in our lives,

00:07:29.100 --> 00:07:30.870
like, my husband and I.

00:07:30.870 --> 00:07:33.390
And we're gonna lean on
them when that happens.

00:07:33.390 --> 00:07:37.290
But for that 11 year old to be approached

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:39.183
by you and say that I'm your mom,

00:07:40.620 --> 00:07:43.650
in her eyes, yes, that would be fantastic.

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:46.710
But those two guys are now
gonna be looked at as someone

00:07:46.710 --> 00:07:49.920
that this little girl
cannot trust anymore.

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:52.770
And that's what's getting me.

00:07:52.770 --> 00:07:55.890
- If you were to tell her
without their permission, right,

00:07:55.890 --> 00:07:57.750
what would be the aftermath of that?

00:07:57.750 --> 00:07:58.950
- Well, I would never.

00:07:58.950 --> 00:08:00.060
Just like you're saying,

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:03.150
they do have strong women
around them already.

00:08:03.150 --> 00:08:07.320
I never want to assert my dominance

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:09.270
because I gave up that right.

00:08:09.270 --> 00:08:12.240
And I gave them the the option

00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:14.430
to choose which women
they want in their lives

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:17.310
to fill that kind of motherly role.

00:08:17.310 --> 00:08:18.930
- I have one quick question for you.

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:20.910
I just wanna ask, like, more clarity

00:08:20.910 --> 00:08:22.770
as someone who doesn't
have that perspective.

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:24.990
Like, why do you think
the child would lose

00:08:24.990 --> 00:08:27.573
trust potentially in the parents?

00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:33.500
- I think it's a huge thing
to keep this away from her.

00:08:33.690 --> 00:08:37.110
I think an 11 year old is very smart.

00:08:37.110 --> 00:08:39.300
It's just very concerning to me, you know,

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:42.900
that this huge thing that will impact

00:08:42.900 --> 00:08:45.540
this little 11-year-old girl's life

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:48.048
doesn't come from her two dads.

00:08:48.048 --> 00:08:49.260
- Okay.
- And will come from you.

00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:51.630
And I'm sure you're a wonderful person.

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:53.820
You have all the great
intention in the world.

00:08:53.820 --> 00:08:57.210
But I think that needs to
be made by the two dads.

00:08:57.210 --> 00:08:58.770
- Your story was very moving, right,

00:08:58.770 --> 00:09:00.690
'cause I want to be a father one day.

00:09:00.690 --> 00:09:02.850
If I were you, I'd be
more assertive and, like,

00:09:02.850 --> 00:09:03.930
get, like, a timeframe.

00:09:03.930 --> 00:09:06.360
Like, say, okay, well, let's
kind of flesh this out.

00:09:06.360 --> 00:09:07.380
- I agree on that.

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:09.690
I do think she should be told.

00:09:09.690 --> 00:09:12.660
But I think she should
be told by her parents.

00:09:12.660 --> 00:09:15.045
- I think there's very
unclarity of what...

00:09:15.045 --> 00:09:17.400
- [Director] Let's wait one minute.

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:19.890
Aurora, what's your thought process here?

00:09:19.890 --> 00:09:23.190
- I have firm faith that
they will meet you halfway,

00:09:23.190 --> 00:09:25.350
and you'll be able to have that moment.

00:09:25.350 --> 00:09:27.840
But you can't do it on your own.

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:29.550
- If I were to put myself in your

00:09:29.550 --> 00:09:32.490
daughter's positions
because I also am adopted,

00:09:32.490 --> 00:09:35.700
if my birth mom came to me
and was like, I'm your mother,

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:38.880
and my parents knew and
didn't tell me first,

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:40.860
that's where I feel like the
distrust would come from.

00:09:40.860 --> 00:09:45.150
Do you feel like you want
to be her mother again?

00:09:45.150 --> 00:09:47.100
Is that, like, part of your intention?

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:48.270
- No.

00:09:48.270 --> 00:09:49.710
I'm a huge ally.

00:09:49.710 --> 00:09:53.040
And I chose gay dads because
I knew that they would be...

00:09:53.040 --> 00:09:54.630
I knew that she would be loved,

00:09:54.630 --> 00:09:58.173
like, what I wasn't
able to do at the time.

00:09:59.130 --> 00:10:02.340
- Thank you for that. That's awesome.

00:10:02.340 --> 00:10:04.170
- But I don't have their
perspective at all.

00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:07.230
I'm a cis (laughs) heterosexual woman.

00:10:07.230 --> 00:10:10.200
And I haven't gone through anything

00:10:10.200 --> 00:10:11.430
that they've gone through.

00:10:11.430 --> 00:10:15.210
- I switched because I
don't think it's a good idea

00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:18.450
for her to tell her daughter.

00:10:18.450 --> 00:10:22.050
I don't think that's okay
because then she will be like,

00:10:22.050 --> 00:10:25.740
you lied to me my whole
life, you know, to her dads

00:10:25.740 --> 00:10:27.510
if she's hearing it from her.

00:10:27.510 --> 00:10:28.590
But at the end of the day,

00:10:28.590 --> 00:10:31.830
it's not like it can't
be the end and be all

00:10:31.830 --> 00:10:34.350
for the rest of her life
though at the same time.

00:10:34.350 --> 00:10:37.504
So yeah, somebody's gotta tell her.

00:10:37.504 --> 00:10:40.421
(compelling music)

00:10:42.655 --> 00:10:44.572
(beep)

00:10:47.130 --> 00:10:49.140
- [Erik] Just that trust issue is just

00:10:49.140 --> 00:10:51.420
so huge for me as a parent.

00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:53.430
- [Kiohona] Definitively, they're lying.

00:10:53.430 --> 00:10:54.480
- [Angelica] Yeah.

00:10:54.480 --> 00:10:56.100
- [Kiohona] And you have to put yourself

00:10:56.100 --> 00:10:58.856
in the position of being lied to.

00:10:58.856 --> 00:11:00.300
When are they gonna be ready?

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:02.160
- [Leesie] She kept talking
about her needs, right?

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:05.280
If she tells the kid
before the parents do,

00:11:05.280 --> 00:11:09.600
the parents can fully be like,
I don't trust you anymore.

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:10.500
- [Angelica] The whole point is

00:11:10.500 --> 00:11:12.060
for her to stand her ground.

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:14.190
Setting all morals aside,
it's legally binding

00:11:14.190 --> 00:11:15.750
that they have to tell her.

00:11:15.750 --> 00:11:19.350
- [Erik] She doesn't see
the whole 360 degree picture

00:11:19.350 --> 00:11:21.720
in that house what's discussed.

00:11:21.720 --> 00:11:25.410
And so for her to come in and
just reveal this huge amount

00:11:25.410 --> 00:11:30.410
of news can be very, very life
damaging to the little girl.

00:11:33.793 --> 00:11:35.430
- I think my last piece of advice

00:11:35.430 --> 00:11:37.980
to you is definitely be
strong in what you want.

00:11:37.980 --> 00:11:39.930
Be direct.

00:11:39.930 --> 00:11:42.060
Redirect the conversation if you have to.

00:11:42.060 --> 00:11:44.010
If you have to take initiative, take it

00:11:44.010 --> 00:11:46.680
because I will say when I didn't,

00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:49.050
I regretted it for the rest of my life.

00:11:49.050 --> 00:11:50.850
And I don't want you to live through that.

00:11:50.850 --> 00:11:53.430
- You're amazing for doing what you did.

00:11:53.430 --> 00:11:56.730
I respect you for that, for specifically,

00:11:56.730 --> 00:11:58.470
you know, placing them in that place.

00:11:58.470 --> 00:12:00.450
But I also think that there's a lot

00:12:00.450 --> 00:12:02.400
more people involved and not just you.

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:05.070
You owe it to her to be honest

00:12:05.070 --> 00:12:07.350
and to be trust and to be patient.

00:12:07.350 --> 00:12:09.480
And you owe it to them to be patient.

00:12:09.480 --> 00:12:11.100
You know, it's been 11 years.

00:12:11.100 --> 00:12:13.050
I think you can be patient a little longer

00:12:13.050 --> 00:12:15.660
and let the dads do it on their time.

00:12:15.660 --> 00:12:17.100
They said that they will.

00:12:17.100 --> 00:12:18.950
And I think that should be respected.

00:12:20.208 --> 00:12:21.686
(compelling music)

00:12:21.686 --> 00:12:22.950
(beep)

00:12:22.950 --> 00:12:25.350
- All right, Paige, have
you made your decision?

00:12:26.670 --> 00:12:27.503
- Yes.

00:12:45.313 --> 00:12:47.396
(laughs)

00:12:48.553 --> 00:12:49.386
- You're amazing.

00:12:49.386 --> 00:12:52.415
- You are great. You're so great.

00:12:52.415 --> 00:12:53.541
- It'll work out for the best.

00:12:53.541 --> 00:12:54.540
- Yeah.
- It will.

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:56.163
- What you did was selfless.

00:12:57.180 --> 00:12:59.100
- I'm excited for you.

00:12:59.100 --> 00:13:02.370
When it's finally out
there and that reconnection

00:13:02.370 --> 00:13:04.020
and all that love that you can give

00:13:04.020 --> 00:13:06.270
to her now, ugh, just openly.

00:13:06.270 --> 00:13:08.493
I'm really excited for her and for you.

00:13:12.046 --> 00:13:13.830
(beep)

00:13:13.830 --> 00:13:15.870
- [Paige] The whole
experience kind of allowed me

00:13:15.870 --> 00:13:19.350
to have all of the perspectives
that I was missing.

00:13:19.350 --> 00:13:23.130
And so to have an
unbiased gay man tell me,

00:13:23.130 --> 00:13:24.480
no, you know, I think we need

00:13:24.480 --> 00:13:26.400
to settle down and kind of go

00:13:26.400 --> 00:13:29.430
at the pace of the parents
was definitely impactful.

00:13:29.430 --> 00:13:31.290
I hope that other birth moms as well

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:34.830
as myself can really feel validated

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:38.340
in our decisions and get our needs met

00:13:38.340 --> 00:13:42.090
even if that means not
getting what we actually want

00:13:42.090 --> 00:13:44.220
but just maybe try to find something else

00:13:44.220 --> 00:13:46.120
that will bring that peace and relief.

